This crate (`symphonia-codec-ldac`) is a pure-Rust LDAC (Sony Bluetooth A2DP) decoder. It is
licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia (see
`LICENSE`).

The bitstream layout, the spectral quantization, the scale-factor and gradient coding, and the
frame header follow the LDAC reference implementation published by Sony Corporation as the AOSP
`external/libldac` encoder (https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/libldac, Copyright
(C) 2003-2017 Sony Corporation), which is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The
following tables in `src/tables.rs` are the verbatim encoder constants (or their direct inverse):

- the scale-factor weighting tables (`gaa_sfcwgt_ldac`),
- the resampled gradient curves (`gaa_resamp_grad_ldac`),
- the scale-factor Huffman codebooks (`sa_hc_sf0_*_ldac`, `sa_hc_sf1_*_ldac`), and
- the 2- and 4-dimensional spectrum code tables (`ga_2dimenc_spec_ldac`, `ga_4dimenc_spec_ldac`,
  emitted here as their decoder-side inverse).

The remaining dequantization step sizes, the spectrum scale, the analysis/synthesis window and the
inverse MDCT are derived from the same reference.

The decoder was cross-checked against the independent open-source `libldacdec` decoder
(https://github.com/hegdi/libldacdec, Copyright (c) 2021 Dirk Helbig, MIT License), which was used
only to validate the decode pipeline, not as a source of code or tables.
